{
  "id": "11799_shimeru",
  "headword": "{占|し}める",
  "reading": "しめる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to occupy; to account for",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "ichidan",
    "stem": "{占|し}め"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to occupy; to hold",
      "explanation": "To physically or abstractly occupy a place, position, or role."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to account for; to make up",
      "explanation": "To constitute a certain proportion or percentage of a whole."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "11799_shimeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{重要|じゅうよう}な{位置|いち}を{占|し}める。",
      "english": "To hold an important position.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11799_shimeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "この{産業|さんぎょう}は{経済|けいざい}の{中|なか}で{大|おお}きな{割合|わりあい}を{占|し}めている。",
      "english": "This industry occupies a large share of the economy.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11799_shimeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}は{私|わたし}の{人生|じんせい}で{特別|とくべつ}な{場所|ばしょ}を{占|し}めている。",
      "english": "She holds a special place in my life.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11799_shimeru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{女性|じょせい}が{全体|ぜんたい}の60%を{占|し}める。",
      "english": "Women account for 60% of the total.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11799_shimeru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{食費|しょくひ}が{支出|ししゅつ}の{大半|たいはん}を{占|し}めている。",
      "english": "Food costs make up the majority of the expenditure.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11799_shimeru_ex6",
      "japanese": "{輸出|ゆしゅつ}に{占|し}める{製造業|せいぞうぎょう}の{割合|わりあい}は{年々|ねんねん}{減少|げんしょう}している。",
      "english": "The proportion of manufacturing in exports is decreasing year by year.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "This is a different word from {閉|し}める (to close) and {締|し}める (to tighten). Sense 2, expressing proportions and percentages, is extremely common in statistics, reports, and news.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n・{割合|わりあい}を{占|し}める: to account for a share\n・{位置|いち}を{占|し}める: to hold a position\n・〜%を{占|し}める: to account for ~%\n・{大半|たいはん}を{占|し}める: to make up the majority",
